THE ONLY WAY ''.l''O PREPARE ABSINTHE WlTH SUG.t\R.
A LA M. PAUL GEFFROY, PARIS.
Place half a cube of sugar in a highball glass three-quarters full of pure
cold water, add about a pony of absinthe and allow the mixture to stand at
least three minutes before stirring; pour the absinthe over the water carefully
so it will float. This method of mixing absinthe and water produces the same
result as dripping.', NULL, NULL, 'highball', 'stirred', NULL, 18, 'unreviewed');
