Orwell wrote that "tea is one of the mainstays of civilisation in this country and causes violent disputes over how it should be made", and his rules cover such matters as the best shape for a teacup, the advisability of ', 1, 5, 15, NULL, 'drink', 0, 0, NULL, 'Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0)', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'mug', 'brewed', NULL, NULL, 'unreviewed');
