Take the whites of any number of eggs and beat
to a stiff froth.

Add 1 y 2 birspoons of sugar to each egg.

Beat the yolks of the eggs separate. Stir well
together and beat till you have a stiff batter.
Add to this as much bicarbonate of soda as
will cover a nickel. Stir up frequently, so that
eggs will not separate or settle.

To serve: Put 1 tablespoonful of batter into
Tom and Jerry mug.

1 jigger rum and brandy mixed.

Fill up with boiling water or milk; grate nutmeg
on top, stir with spoon and serve.', NULL, NULL, 'mug', 'built_hot', 'grated nutmeg', 18, 'unreviewed');
